<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prague Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pražský hrad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> Castle is a vast castle complex above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vltava">Vltava</a> in Prague, founded in the late 9th century by the Přemyslid duke Bořivoj. It has been the seat of Bohemian dukes and kings, of Holy Roman emperors, and of Czechoslovak and Czech presidents, and contains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-vitus-cathedral">St Vitus Cathedral</a>. In March 1939 Hitler proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prague-castle.jpg" alt="Prague Castle" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tilman2007 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl%C5%AFv_most_Praha,_Star%C3%A9_M%C4%9Bsto_20170810_007.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
